# LeakSanitizer suppressions for known non-project noise.
#
# SDL2 opens a D-Bus session-bus connection at SDL_Init() time (desktop
# idle-inhibit/power-management integration) - see the call chain under
# Timer::Initialize() in every leak report below. libdbus deliberately
# caches this "shared connection" for the process lifetime instead of
# freeing it, and whether LeakSanitizer sees it as still-reachable or
# not depends on a timing race with that connection's own background
# thread teardown relative to when the leak check runs - not on
# anything this project's code does (confirmed: identical shutdown
# code path regardless of how the app is quit). Usage: LSAN_OPTIONS=
# suppressions=lsan.supp ./bin/BGEmu ...
leak:libdbus-1.so
leak:libSDL2
